        // Idea: Call play() twice from the same player. On C, if first call wins, pot resets to 0, second call can have pot 10 again. On M, pot is forced to 0 before the win check, causing any winning call to revert, but if both calls are non-winning, pot is always 0. But we cannot control randomness without manipulating block.timestamp etc., but we can try many seeds.
